596,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00066,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Immunocore Holdings plc, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the development and commercialization of immunomodulating medicines for patients with cancer, infectious diseases, and autoimmune disease in the United States, Europe, and internationally. The company offers KIMMTRAK for the treatment of unresectable or metastatic uveal melanoma. It also develops oncology programs, including tebentafusp which is in Phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of advanced cutaneous melanoma and adjuvant uveal melanoma; brenetafusp which is in Phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of first-line advanced cutaneous melanoma and in Phase 1/2 clinical trial for the treatment of various tumor types; IMC-R117C which is in Phase 1/2 clinical trial for the treatment of advanced solid tumors, such as colorectal cancer; and IMC-P115C which is in Phase 1 clinical trial for patients with tumors that express PRAME. In addition, the company is involved in the development of IMC-M113V which is in Phase 1 clinical trial for a potential functional cure of human immunodeficiency virus; and IMC-I109V which is in Phase 1 clinical trial for a potential functional cure of hepatitis B virus. Further, it develops IMC-S118AI which is in pre-investigation stage for the treatment of type 1 diabetes; and IMC-U120AI which is in pre-investigation stage for the treatment of atopic dermatitis. The company was founded in 1999 and is headquartered in Abingdon, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Bahija  Jallal Ph.D. | CEO & Executive Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 524 people. Revenue per employee of $763K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 27%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $72K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Immunocore Holdings plc is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.6B market cap on $400M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $15M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 8559% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":85.5924066924067},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5409678.91},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"am